## Common User Intents

**How do I set up a server?**
- Purchase a BisectOne plan, select a game and location, and the server deploys automatically via ServerSpawn — no manual configuration required to get started.
- Log in to the Starbase Panel at https://games.bisecthosting.com to manage settings, install mods, and configure the server.
- Full setup guides: https://help.bisecthosting.com

**Can I switch games without buying a new plan?**
- Yes. BisectOne supports game swapping across 100+ titles on a single subscription.
- Minimum RAM requirements apply per game. Check the game's page for minimums.
- Use the Instance Manager to save your current setup before swapping to preserve progress.
- Details: https://www.bisecthosting.com/bisectone

**What games are supported?**
- 100+ titles including Minecraft (Java & Bedrock), Hytale, Terraria, ARK: Survival Evolved, Valheim, Rust, Palworld, Project Zomboid, Farming Simulator 25, Vintage Story, Garry's Mod, and more.
- Full catalog: https://www.bisecthosting.com/game-server-hosting

**What modpacks are available for Minecraft?**
- 2,300+ modpacks available via one-click install in the Starbase Panel (FTB, CurseForge, Technic, and others).
- Modpack library: https://www.bisecthosting.com/modpack-server-hosting

**What is the Starbase Panel?**
- BisectHosting's custom game server control panel. Includes file manager, live console, config editor, backup manager, scheduled tasks, FTP access, and live performance metrics.
- Overview: https://www.bisecthosting.com/control-panel

**How do I contact support?**
- Live chat or ticket via: https://help.bisecthosting.com
- Available 24/7/365. Average ticket response under 15 minutes.

**Where are the servers located?**
- 21 locations across North America, Europe, Asia, and Australia.
- Location list and latency checker: https://www.bisecthosting.com/locations

**What is the difference between an instance and a backup?**
- An instance is a saved, independent server environment (game, modpack, world, config) that you can switch to and run. It is active and switchable.
- A backup is a snapshot of server files used to restore data after an error or loss. It is not an active environment.
- BisectOne base plans include 2 instance slots and 2 backup slots, sharing a 40 GB storage pool.

**What is BisectBoost?**
- An account-wide add-on (not a separate plan) that adds: extra instance slots, additional backup storage, premium subdomains, and access to temporary RAM boosting.
- It supplements BisectOne but does not replace it.

